107 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (The implemented solution uses Python and accepts the order N and a partially filled Latin square from the user. Empty cells are represented by 0. Before searching, the program validates the input by checking symbol ranges and duplicate values in rows and columns. During the search, it computes candidate values for empty cells, applies constraint propagation, selects the most constrained cell using the Minimum Remaining Values \(MRV\) heuristic, and uses backtracking with early pruning.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
108 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 71 0 R
/E (The implementation also verifies the completed square, measures actual execution time, and reports solver statistics such as recursive calls, assignments, backtracks, and pruned branches. The uploaded notebook demonstrates a successful run in which a partially filled order-4 square is completed without backtracking and the final row and column constraints are verified.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
