317 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (The project successfully implements Latin Square Completion as a constraint satisfaction problem using backtracking. The uploaded implementation combines row and column uniqueness checking with constraint propagation, MRV- based variable selection, pruning, final verification, execution-time measurement, and solver statistics. The recorded run demonstrates a valid completion and confirms all required constraints.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
318 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 79 0 R
/E (The approach satisfies the requirements of Q39 by clearly defining the uniqueness constraints, analyzing how those constraints reduce the search space, developing a backtracking solution, applying constraint propagation, and justifying correctness and computational complexity. The method is practical for demonstrating constraint-based problem solving and illustrates why intelligent search decisions are important in combinatorial problems.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
